just landed  in belfast  awaiting the queen's arrival later on  today  and yeah it was in the last 20 minutes  that we were told by buckingham palace  that unfortunately the queen is now no  longer able to come and as you said  there in their statement they make it  very clear that  um she's taking this advice um from the  royal medical household they've said to  her that she has to rest for the next  few days um we're also being told though  that she is in uh good spirits but in  many ways it's probably  not surprising that they told her to  take a rest because the last couple of  weeks have been  incredibly busy when you consider that  she is 95 years old yes she has all of  the best possible help around her and  she lives a very privileged life but for  95 years old she has been undergoing a  very busy work schedule so just last  night we saw her  at the global investment summit  reception that was being hosted at  windsor castle actually she seemed in  fantastic spirits  i watched all of the pictures  of her meeting and greeting the various  business leaders that boris johnson  number 10 had wanted invited to wins the  castle and there was a wonderful moment  where she stopped and spoke to  john kerry and said oh i saw you on the  telly last week referring to the fact  that she'd seen john kerry had recorded  a video message for prince william's  earth shot prize um of course now that  she is older of course now that prince  philip is no longer by her side we are  now increasingly seeing other members of  the royal family around her so also last  night we saw  prince charles and  prince william but yeah last night's  engagements at windsor castle was just  one of i would say over half a dozen  engagements that she's done in the last  couple of weeks um she's returned from  from scotland where she spent her summer  holidays in balmoral um  of course up in scotland before she flew  back down  to england  she opened the scottish parliament gave  a speech there  she then traveled back down  to windsor we saw her hosting the  commonwealth baton relay on the  forecourt at buckingham palace and she  also last week i was there as well she  went to open  the welsh parliament and then yeah as i  said last night she also hosted that  global investment summit so at 95 years  old she certainly has not slowed down  and i think whenever you speak to the  palace they make the point that it's the  queen who who drives this this busy  schedule she's the one that has wanted  to get back out and about especially  when you consider that because of covid  for around 18 months  that schedule of royal engagements and  meeting and greeting all of that had to  come to a complete standstill a schedule  that she's been so used to carrying out  throughout her nearly 70 year reign she  was there at windsor castle within that  bubble being protected  from everybody because of covid and so i  think since all of the restrictions have  started to lift she has been desperate  with other men's royal family to get out  and about congratulate those who've gone  above and beyond when it comes to to  helping their communities when it comes  to covid but yeah i think of course  there will be understandably worry about  the queen and the fact that she is now  being told to rest up she is 95 years  old but i think just to reiterate the  palace is saying that  she has reluctantly accepted his medical  advice to rest for the next few days in  some ways maybe that ties in with the  fact that yesterday we also heard that  she'd turned down a prize of the aldi of  the year because she basically didn't  feel that she feels old enough for that  um we're also told that the queen is in  good spirits she is disappointed that  she's no longer able to travel to  northern ireland over the next couple of  days but also what we're being guided on  is that this is not covered related  and uh rhiannon as you say she's been  around the united kingdom recently in  scotland and in wales uh can you what  can you tell us about what she was due  to do in northern ireland  so we understand that this afternoon she  was due to visit uh hillsborough castle  hillsborough recently has been given the  honor of being renamed royal hilfr so  she was she was due to  to mark that and congratulate those  who've been part of  that important campaign to make that  happen and also as we saw in wales and  in scotland she was due to meet up with  some  covered heroes as i said it's been a  really important point for her that she  gets  gets around the country gets out and  about and sends other members of the  royal family out and about to  congratulate everyone who's really gone  above and beyond when it comes to  working um throughout the pandemic and  also there were reports that she was due  to attend a very important um  church ceremony which is due to take  place tomorrow um recognizing the  centenary um of northern ireland  the palace were not commenting uh on  that but because the president of  ireland michael d higgins  last month has said that he wouldn't be  attending  that service there has been a great deal  of chatter over here about whether or  not the queen would attend but yeah as  we now know uh under medical advice the  queen has been told that she cannot come  to northern ireland and yeah the doctors  around her clearly have said you've had  a busy couple of weeks and of course  don't forget really importantly in a  couple of weeks the queen is due to host  the opening reception for cop26 we have  heard so much to remember the royal  family  over the last couple of weeks  about climate change about our  environmental responsibilities and i  think they the palace and number 10 will  be desperate for her to be  at the start of cop26 the royal family  in a way the ultimate welcoming party  really helping to set that tone ahead of  some difficult discussions ahead up in  glasgow but certainly welcoming the  delegates  and makes them feel welcome here in the  uk

